cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Goyal"
    given-names: "Naman"
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Science (IISc), Bangalore"
title: "SMVac: Standard Model electroweak vacuum stability — analytical approximations versus a numerical reference"
version: 2.0.0-dev
url: "https://github.com/namangoyal31/SMVac"
repository-code: "https://github.com/namangoyal31/SMVac"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible computational investigation of the tree-level O(4) bounce action of the RG-improved Standard Model
  potential (three-loop running, one-loop or MS-bar effective quartic), computed with a validated numerical
  reference (spectral collocation). The reference is used to test established analytical approximations: the
  Fubini-Lipatov formula (a rigorous lower bound), the first- and second-order running corrections of Espinosa
  (2020), and resummed and variational estimates. The test includes their breakdown near the absolute-stability
  boundary. Phase diagrams of the (M_h, M_t) plane from the numerical bounce show the measured masses with their
  1 sigma and 2 sigma regions. The work does not compute the one-loop decay rate.
keywords:
  - vacuum stability
  - phase diagram
  - Higgs boson
  - renormalization group
  - bounce action
  - vacuum decay
